<h2>Pass 1 — Conceptual</h2>
<p>Entities and relationships in business language. No attributes.</p>
<pre><code>Order *--* LineItem
Order &gt;--1 Customer
LineItem &gt;--1 Item</code></pre>
<h2>Pass 2 — Logical</h2>
<p>Attributes, keys, cardinality, 3NF, tech-agnostic.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Entity</th><th>Attributes</th><th>Keys</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Order</td><td>id, customer_id, status, total, created_at</td><td>PK(id), FK(customer_id)</td></tr><tr><td>LineItem</td><td>order_id, item_id, qty, unit_price</td><td>PK(order_id, item_id), FK(order_id), FK(item_id)</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Pass 3 — Physical</h2>
<p>Engine-specific types, indexes, partitions.</p>
<pre><code class="language-sql">CREATE TABLE orders (
  id          uuid PRIMARY KEY,
  customer_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES customers(id),
  status      order_status NOT NULL,
  total       numeric(12,2) NOT NULL,
  created_at  timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);
CREATE INDEX orders_customer_id_created_at ON orders (customer_id, created_at DESC);</code></pre>
